WIRE.md §2.2 rule 5, SPEC §3.1 (DECISIONS 332): a load under an optional root absent on this machine is
E7009 at the load, naming the root; the same load under an optional root this machine has is read as
any load is, so the verdict depends on the project and its roots, never on a silent skip.
-- check-only --
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    client: "../absent-client"
    lib: "../lib"
  }
  optional_roots: [client, lib]
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Row.
record Row {
  /// Label.
  label: String
}

/// Gone.
let gone: [Row] = load("@client/rows.json")

/// Here.
let here: [Row] = load("@lib/rows.json")
-- ../lib/rows.json --
[{"label": "x"}]
-- findings.txt --
error[E7009]  a/a.canon:11:19
  cannot read @client/rows.json: root @client is optional and not present on this machine; clone it or point to it in project.local.canon, or check only the packages that do not read it

